%% Source for Fig. 5.4 (sec:design-loop). Render to vector PDF (adaptive-loop.pdf), e.g.:
%% Render with: ./render-diagrams.sh  (mmdc + mermaid-config.json + --pdfFit, keeps text legible at \linewidth)
%% Two distinct front-end surfaces: the participant reading surface (text only)
%% and the researcher console (mirror + fixation heat map + saccade overlay).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant E as Eye tracker
    participant P as Participant reading surface
    participant C as Backend core
    participant M as Researcher console
    actor O as Researcher

    loop Adaptive cycle — while the session is live
        E->>C: gaze sample (raw)
        activate C
        C-->>P: live gaze (real-time channel)
        C-->>M: live gaze (real-time channel)
        P->>C: reading observation (gaze → token)
        C->>C: analysis — project fixations, saccades, regressions
        C-->>M: analysed events — fixation heat map, saccade overlay
        Note over M,O: the researcher sees where and how<br/>the participant is reading
        C->>C: decision — evaluate (built-in / external)
        alt advisory mode
            C-->>M: intervention proposal
            O->>C: approve / reject (informed by the overlays)
        else autonomous mode
            Note over C: applied without the operator
        end
        C->>C: validate, then commit at controlled boundary
        Note right of C: an anchor restores<br/>the reader's position
        C-->>P: adapted text + intervention event (re-render)
        C-->>M: adapted text mirrored to the console
        C->>C: checkpoint
        deactivate C
    end
